# A parser's loop: read a code unit, leave at the first that is no digit, else multiply and add. The unit and the value stay 32-bit integers, and `| 0` takes the overflow checks away.
# `code < 48 || code > 57` is one subtraction, one unsigned comparison and one branch.
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 1
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[unit]] = Load8Z(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:characters8, {{*}}:GetStringCodeUnit)
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[digit]] = Add(b@[[unit]], $-48(
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isNoDigit]] = Above(b@[[digit]], $9(
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isNoDigit]], Terminal,
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[tenfold]] = Mul(b@{{*}}, $10(
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[sum]] = Add(b@[[unit]], b@[[tenfold]],
# CHECK: Int32 b@{{*}} = Add(b@[[sum]], $-48(
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# No range check, no test of the width or for a rope, no poll, no number that is not an integer, no check for overflow.
# HOT-LABEL: steps by 1
# HOT-NOT: isLoopPoll
# HOT-NOT: Reads:StringImpl
# HOT-NOT: Reads:JSRopeString
# HOT-NOT: ExitsSideways
# HOT-NOT: IToD
# HOT-NOT: Double
# HOT-NOT: CheckMul
# HOT-NOT: CheckAdd
# HOT-LABEL: end of loop
# X64: instructions: 7, patchpoints: 1, {{*}} steps by 1
# ARM64: instructions: 7, patchpoints: 1, {{*}} steps by 1
